# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your real key.
# `.env` is gitignored so the key never leaves your machine.

# =============================================================================
# Which provider the SDK chapters use.
#
#   gemini  (default) -> Chat Completions API, free. Use this for the whole
#                        curriculum. Everything below under "Gemini" applies.
#   openai            -> Responses API, PAID. Needed only for the hosted-tools
#                        chapter (web search, file search, code interpreter),
#                        which cannot run on Chat Completions.
#
# See RESPONSES_VS_CHATCOMPLETIONS.md for why the default is what it is.
# Check which one you are on:  uv run python -m shared.models
# =============================================================================
AGENT_PROVIDER=gemini

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini — the free path. Required.
#
# These keep the OPENAI_* names because the OpenAI Python SDK reads them and
# every `from_scratch/` script builds its client from them directly.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/

# NOT every Gemini model can run this curriculum. From Chapter 3 on, the spine
# uses `output_type=` (a JSON response format) TOGETHER WITH tools, and some
# models support each separately but refuse the combination:
#
#   400 INVALID_ARGUMENT
#   "Function calling with a response mime type: 'application/json' is unsupported"
#
# `gemini-2.5-flash` fails that way. Verified working as of Aug 2026, with the
# daily free-tier cap each one actually carries:
#
#   gemini-3.5-flash-lite   500 / day   <- the default. Only one that fits a dataset run
#   gemini-3.6-flash        (check)
#   gemini-3.5-flash         20 / day   <- fine for demos, too small for a dataset
#
# Before trusting a new model with a 15-minute dataset run, spend one request:
# point an agent with ONE tool and ONE `output_type=` at it and see if it answers.
MODEL_NAME=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# THE FREE-TIER LIMIT THAT WILL ACTUALLY STOP YOU
# -----------------------------------------------
# There are two, and the famous one is not the one that bites:
#
#   ~15 requests / MINUTE  -> annoying. Wait a minute, carry on.
#   N requests / DAY       -> stops your work until tomorrow.
#
# The daily cap is quotaId `GenerateRequestsPerDayPerProjectPerModel-FreeTier`,
# and the last two words are the useful part: the bucket is per PROJECT and per
# MODEL. So when you exhaust one model for the day, switching MODEL_NAME to a
# different Gemini model gives you a fresh bucket immediately. A second API key
# from the SAME project does not -- it shares the exhausted one.
#
# **N IS NOT THE SAME FOR EVERY MODEL, and the difference is enormous.** Measured
# Aug 2026, by reading `quotaValue` out of the 429 body:
#
#   gemini-3.5-flash-lite   500 / day   <- the curriculum's default, for this reason
#   gemini-3.5-flash         20 / day   <- one dataset run does not fit
#
# A 20/day model cannot complete a single golden-dataset run (60-90 requests), so
# "switch to any other model" is bad advice on its own. Switch to a model you have
# checked. The number is printed in every 429: read `quotaValue`.
#
# Switch to a model from the verified list above. Reaching for an arbitrary one
# mid-run costs you the run: `gemini-2.5-flash` was picked as a fresh bucket once
# and failed every case with a 400 that has nothing to do with quota.
#
# You do NOT have to edit this file to switch. `load_dotenv()` does not override
# variables already in the environment, so a shell prefix wins for one command:
#
#   MODEL_NAME=gemini-3.6-flash uv run python .../check_multiturn.py
#
# Budget: one golden-dataset run is roughly 60-90 requests. You get about five
# or six full runs a day per model. Ordinary chapter work costs far less.
#
# If you are running datasets repeatedly (instructors, mostly), ~$5 of OpenAI
# credit and AGENT_PROVIDER=openai removes the problem entirely. Students never
# need this.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI — the paid path. Leave blank unless you are on the hosted-tools chapter.
#
# Deliberately a DIFFERENT variable name from OPENAI_API_KEY above. If they
# shared a name, flipping AGENT_PROVIDER would send your Gemini key to
# api.openai.com and fail with a confusing 401.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_PLATFORM_API_KEY=sk-your_real_paid_openai_key_here
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o
